comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T20:58:39.011Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence for the registry-not-prose acceptance criterion: scripts/release/gate-registry.mjs discovers the gate inventory by regex over GitHub workflow step NAMES — GATE_STEP_PATTERN matches /\\b(build|typecheck|test|gates?|check|scan|analysis|benchmark|verify|dogfood|release pipeline|enforce|coverage|quality)\\b/i and NON_GATE_STEP_PATTERN excludes steps beginning setup|install|checkout|download|upload|restore|record|resolve|alert|create github release. A gate's identity is therefore its human-written title, so renaming a step silently changes the inventory and adding a gate whose step name avoids the vocabulary makes it invisible to its own ownership registry. Same failure shape as pm-dqtzva (release gate classifying production errors by message prose) on a different surface: enforcement reading prose rather than a declared contract."
  "2026-08-10T21:22:56.873Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-08-10: reused canonical gate item after all-status duplicate search and fully read the closed registry, message-classification, and deterministic commit-view lineages. This tranche makes registry identity and machine verdicts first-class SDK/CLI contracts."
  "2026-08-10T23:01:04.880Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence 2026-08-11: assurance is a first-class core CLI command and shared SDK action, PmClient method, one-shot runtime action, and MCP transport with registry CRUD, trigger-bound gate runs, dry-run semantics, bounded mutation projections, deterministic verdicts, and exit codes. Runtime contracts expose all seven canonical flags and generated CLI/MCP/public-surface snapshots were refreshed. Lint, typecheck, contract, token-surface, package, dogfood, and 7,201-test exact-coverage gates passed. The aggregate release pipeline stopped only at hosted-analysis because DeepScan cannot have an exact-head result before this branch is committed and pushed; that provider result remains required on the PR head."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T23:01:05.479Z","harness:codex","Registering a new core command is incomplete until runtime-contract enumeration, aggregate SDK exports, tool schemas, generated fixtures, and token-surface baselines all identify the same command; a working parser alone is not contract completeness."
